{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression coefficient linear regression coefficient","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Coefficient.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Coefficient","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Linear Regression Analysis]] · [[Linear Model Design and Contrasts]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","Indicator Variable","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression coefficient linear regression coefficient","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Coefficient.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Coefficient","heading":"Linear Regression Coefficient","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A linear regression coefficient is the estimated change in a continuous outcome associated with a one-unit increase in a predictor while the other model terms remain fixed. For an [[Indicator Variable]], it is the adjusted mean difference from the reference group.\n\nIts sign gives direction and its magnitude remains in outcome units. The standard error, confidence interval, and p-value describe estimation uncertainty, while subject-matter context determines whether the change is important.\n\nThe source emphasizes that a coefficient's meaning follows from its design-matrix column. With an indicator, it may represent a group difference; with a continuous predictor, a slope; and with a product column, an interaction adjustment to another effect.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","Indicator Variable","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"linear regression coefficient linear regression coefficient","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Linear Regression Coefficient.md","fileName":"Linear Regression Coefficient.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Linear Regression Coefficient","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf]]\n\n[[dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Linear Regression Analysis","Linear Model Design and Contrasts","Indicator Variable","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}